+### `os-window-always-on-top-changed` — Stable
+
+Fires when a window's [Keep on top](#keep-on-top) state flips, from the title-bar pin or from `windowManager.setAlwaysOnTop()`. Not fired when a window opens already kept on top (session restore, `alwaysOnTop: true` in the open config), and not fired for a call that leaves the state as it was.
+
+**`detail` shape:**
+
+```typescript
+{
+    windowId:    string,
+    alwaysOnTop: boolean,   // the new state
+}
+```
+
+Companion `wp.hooks` action: `HOOKS.WINDOW_ALWAYS_ON_TOP_CHANGED` (`os.window.always-on-top-changed`).
+
+---
+
