+<a id="keep-on-top"></a>
+**Keep on top.** A window kept on top paints above every window that is not, even when another window is focused or opened after it. The user toggles it from the pin in the title bar (the `core/always-on-top` control); code calls `manager.setAlwaysOnTop( windowId, enabled )` and reads `win.alwaysOnTop`.
+
+- **Focus is unchanged.** Focusing a window under a kept-on-top one still focuses it (it gets the keyboard and the focused title bar); it just paints below. Focus order and `manager.getFocused()` are what they would be without the flag.
+- **Several at once.** Windows kept on top stack among themselves in focus order. Turning the flag off puts the window back into normal stacking at its place in that order.
+- **Children follow their owner.** A [child window](#child-windows--stable) of a kept-on-top owner is kept on top with it, so ownership still holds.
+- **Fullscreen still wins.** A fullscreen window covers the viewport above every window, kept on top or not.
+- **Session.** The flag is saved with the window's session entry (`alwaysOnTop: true`) and restored on reload. Passing `alwaysOnTop: true` to `open()` / `openNew()` opens a window already kept on top.
+
+Each change fires [`os-window-always-on-top-changed`](#os-window-always-on-top-changed) and the `os.window.always-on-top-changed` action.
